w how to check it here is a [guide](https://nvidia.custhelp.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/5429/~/running-vulkan-info#:~:text=In%20the%20command%20line%2C%20type,information%20installed%20on%20your%20PC.).\n\nYou could also try to update your Vulkan if its not the latest version and see if that fixed it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2701341894/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2702190073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103603#issuecomment-2702190073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103603","id":2702190073,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hECX5","user":{"login":"JojoEngineer","id":109865068,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoxobA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109865068?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer","html_url":"https://github.com/JojoEngineer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JojoEngineer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-05T22:08:12Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T22:08:12Z","body":"> Do you know what your vulkan version is? If you want to know how to check it here is a [guide](https://nvidia.custhelp.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/5429/~/running-vulkan-info#:~:text=In%20the%20command%20line%2C%20type,information%20installed%20on%20your%20PC.).\n> \n> You could also try to update your Vulkan if its not the latest version and see if that fixed it.\n\nThat is a good point that I overlooked!\nSo I downloaded the latest version 1.4.304.1 but the same issue still occurred.\nI decided to debug vulkan by running a test using vkvia command and it was failing on the vkCube test. After looking at the output of that test I noticed that some layers were being used by other programs, in my case was WonderShare Demo Creator, it was using an outdated layer that was making vulkan fail the test. After removing that program from my PC the vkvia test was successful. I then opened up Godot and everything is working!!\n\nNot sure how that is related and why I wasnt having the issue before until now. What a weird bug to have. Well I suggest if anyone having this same issue with Vulkan to run the vkvia test and look at the logs. May encounter the same issue I had. \n\nThanks for the reply @ArtinGaming \nGonna close this ticket.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2702190073/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]